g1-review.imperative:
Independently verify the g1 diff against ADMIRAL_RULING-1.md R1-R4. Reproduce every pasted command yourself; take the implementer's word for nothing. Check specifically:
(a) the governor never REFUSES anywhere it previously permitted -- ENUMERATE the refusal paths rather than sampling them;
(b) R2 holds TOTALLY: feed the checkout's real session ids through the normalizer and confirm EVERY one yields a usable key, including slash-bearing ids, null, and the literal '$SID'. A normalizer that rejects even one is the invisible-coverage-loss failure this ruling exists to prevent;
(c) R3 holds: a LEASELESS checklist still reads the unowned gauge.json and trips exactly as today -- and, separately, that a LEASED checklist with no owner-keyed gauge returns None rather than falling back to the shared file;
(d) R4 holds: #488's exact shape (an Admiral's spine.json plus its latitude-interrogation.json in one work directory) still WRITES, and two distinct owners in one work directory BOTH write;
(e) R1's limit is respected: #601's timestamp comparison is still present and still fires on the sequential relaunch case, and the result does not claim identity-not-time is complete;
(f) the owner key has ONE definition, or the departure is argued -- two definitions across the hook/engine process boundary is a silent-drift hazard, not a style question;
(g) the blast-radius enumeration is complete and its COUNT is stated -- RE-RUN the enumeration yourself, because an under-inclusive sweep reports clean precisely because it never reached the interesting items;
(h) the red-before/green-after evidence drives the real reader and a real gauge file, not a patched _read_gauge;
(i) no fenced file was edited.
Note for the record: this gate's own postcondition is satisfied by ANY verdict including BLOCK -- that is deliberate. Discrimination lives at g1-integrate c2, which requires APPROVE.
